From: starbite <starbite@local>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: 0446-sweet-a64e-hot-pcs.patch - every arm64e-emulation trap's PC
 goes into the hot-site table, so "STARLTE LSE hot:" names the hottest emulated instructions

S3z4 2026-11-13: ~55k traps/s from WindowServer and ControlCenter on the idle desktop, nearly all
"other", cost the kernel ~60 % of a core. Diagnostic. Applies on 0445. Kernel seq1r = seq1q + this.
---

--- a/osfmk/arm64/sweet_a64e.c	2026-11-13 21:06:28
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/sweet_a64e.c	2026-11-13 21:06:28
@@ -630,6 +630,10 @@
 	}
 	sweet_a64e_count_pid();
 	uint64_t pc = get_saved_state_pc(ss);
+	/* 0446: every arm64e trap's PC goes into the hot-site table too ("STARLTE LSE hot:" every 10 s): S3z4
+	 * 2026-11-13, ~55k traps/s from WindowServer and ControlCenter, nearly all "other", cost the kernel ~60 %
+	 * of a core on the idle desktop; which instructions? (shared-cache PCs: one slide for every process) */
+	lse_site(pc);
 
 	if ((w & 0xFFFFFBFF) == 0xD65F0BFF) {                   /* RETAA, RETAB */
 		set_saved_state_pc(ss, reg_get(ss, 30, false));
